  "body": "# Associated User Story\n\nAs an officer/manager creating an event, I want the location proximity to be something like 250 feet (not in meters), and able to adjust. \n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n\n**Officers and managers can set an event’s location proximity in feet, and adjust it as needed**\n\n- Sunny: An officer or manager creates or edits an event and sees a “Location proximity” field labeled in feet, pre-filled with a default of 250 feet. They can change it to any value within the allowed range (e.g., 100 to 1,000 feet) and save. The system stores the value, shows it in feet on the event details page, and uses it when checking whether a member is close enough to the event location. Changing the value later updates the check for that event without affecting other events.\n\n- Rainy: The officer or manager enters a value that is blank, non-numeric, zero or negative, or outside the allowed range. They see a clear message next to the field explaining the problem (e.g., “Enter a proximity between 100 and 1,000 feet”) instead of a blank page or a silent failure. The event is not saved until the value is fixed, and any previously saved proximity stays unchanged. A regular member who tries to create or edit an event, or change its proximity, is blocked (officers and managers only).\n\nDefinition of Done -\nA story is done when its acceptance criteria are met and every item in the team PR template is satisfied:\n(A) code review by a non-author, coding standard met, RuboCop checked with output/CI link, and setup changes documented;\n(B) the human-only maintainability checks (meaningful comments and names, skinny controllers, thin views, DRY, Rails conventions, foreign keys, enums, nested routes);\n(C) tests added or updated and passing. Any deferred items or RuboCop exclusions are explained in Section D of the PR.\n(D) Deferred (not this story)\n- Help-page rewrite beyond unit/range wording (incl. screenshot captions), reason: out of scope for this story.",
